{"claim": "The camera settings dialog always shows both sections (Camera via camera_settings, Recording via dvr_settings); every save with DVR on restarts recording (settings.rs stops and restarts the capture), so the Camera section says 'Saving restarts recording.' while the DVR switch is on.", "detail": "Session 3 C6 (2026-11-06). The dialog is mounted fresh on every open, so it refetches camera/settings each time. Save sends only real values (a missing field must not overwrite a stored setting with null), including storage, which start_recording reads on each start, so a new directory takes effect at once. A failed save (top-level err, or the command's own {status:err} wrapped as data) shows in the sticky footer and keeps the dialog open. Switches are class-based (no ids) so two tiles' dialogs don't cross-toggle. While recording, camera_settings previews last_keyframe instead of a second capture, and its preview loop stops when the dialog is hidden.", "tags": "camera,settings,dialog,dvr,C6,C5", "source": {"lib": "camera", "ctl": "dvr_settings", "facet": "js", "hash": "0294888c3db540c2"}, "confidence": "high", "time": 1793967587369},
{"end": true}]
